X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Montclairfoundation Calendar Of Events": "https://montclairfoundation.org/event/mill-birds-and-art/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:montclairfoundation_calendar_of_events
X-SOURCE:Montclair Foundation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260618T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260618T143000
DTSTAMP:20260618T004625
CREATED:20260331T145812Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260331T225152Z
UID:10007534-1781789400-1781793000@montclairfoundation.org
SUMMARY:MILL Birds and Art
DESCRIPTION:These classes are a Partner Program with the Montclair Institute for Lifelong Learning. To register please visit: http://schedulesplus.com/montclair/kiosk \nThursdays\, 1:30 PM – 2:30 PM \nJune 18 – Birds and Art – We’ll learn about some of our favorite resident birds at Van Vleck with Naturalist Jenny Aley and discuss their summer activities. We will also explore our creative side with a simple painting or sketching activity that will help us identify some of our beautiful native birds. No experience necessary – all levels of birders and artists welcome! (Indoor Program) \nJune 25th – Mindfulness in the Garden – Jodi Brooks will guide us through very gentle stretching & breathwork\, and an outdoor contemplative garden walk. This is a practice of slowing down\, cultivating quiet and paying attention to our senses. All levels are welcome. No experience needed. Cold or rainy weather – class will be held indoors\, with a short walk outdoors (weather permitting). (Outdoor Program\, indoors if inclement weather)
URL:https://montclairfoundation.org/event/mill-birds-and-art/
CATEGORIES:Classes,Adults
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://montclairfoundation.org/content/uploads/2024/06/hummingbird-Veronika-Andrews1280.webp
END:VEVENT
