SUMMARY:🚶Yanticaw Park Nutley
DESCRIPTION:Let's Walk!!\nMeet along Park Drive in Nutley near the Orechio
  Sports Complex. We'll walk about 3.5 mile through scenic Yanticaw Park\, 
 up to Kingsland St. and back. The path is paved and mostly flat.\n\nPlease
  check the event page beforehand in case of any changes. Inclement weather
  will cancel the walk.\n\nThe Yanticaw Park is an Essex County-owned park 
 in Nutley\, New Jersey. It is located between Centre Street and Chestnut S
 treet\, extending west to Passaic Avenue.\n\nEssex County began purchasing
  land in 1911 for creation of the park. Wetlands in the park were drained\
 , and a dam was set up to form a lake. The park was completed in 1914. In 
 1962\, the lake\, containing a small island was drained and a channel was 
 dug as a continuation of the natural third river from the south.\n\nPLEASE
  ARRIVE 5 MINUTES **EARLY** SO WE CAN START TO WALK ON TIME\n\nDisclaimer:
  If you join us for a walk/hike\, please understand that you are responsib
 le for your own preparedness and well-being and will hold no one else liab
 le in case of injury or mishap. Walk/hike will be canceled in the event of
  extreme weather.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lets-walkprogram/events/315270460/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260615T143854Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260615T143854Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
