DTEND:20260620T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260620T000000Z
SUMMARY:Juneteenth Block Party
DESCRIPTION:Montclair Public Library\, Friends of the Howe House and 
 Montclair Township present a community celebration of\nfreedom with food\, 
 fun\, friends\, family\, and activities for all ages! Join us for games\, 
 face painting\, balloon art\,\nperformances\, dancing and more. Bring your 
 own chair and clack fan!\n\n“Come Celebrate With Me” is a year-long 
 series of programming honoring 100 years of observing Black history in 
 America. Founded in 1926 by Carter G. Woodson\, Negro History Week evolved 
 into Black History Month\, opening the door for additional annual 
 commemorations such as Juneteenth\, Black Music Month\, Caribbean Heritage 
 Month\, Kwanzaa and more.\n\nMontclair Public Library will honor the 
 centennial of these commemorations in 2026 through a series of programs 
 designed to engage and connect participants while highlighting and 
 celebrating the experiences and contributions of people of African descent 
 in the United States.\n\nMade possible by funds from the New Jersey State 
 Council on the Arts\, a partner agency of the National Endowment for the 
 Arts
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Main - Library Plaza\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Library":MAILTO:events@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Adult Services, Children's Programs
UID:LibCal-10306-16608932
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16608932
END:VEVENT
