DTSTAMP:20260706T000000Z
SUMMARY:Pepe Santana and Grupo Inkhay: Free Live Andean Concert NEW
DESCRIPTION:Note: This is a paid Adult School class. Click here to 
 register.\n\n\n	\n		\n			\n			This is the kickoff for the Paved with 
 Promise suitcase exhibition\, which will be installed in Montclair Public 
 Library's lobby on July 1 by the Folklife Center of Northern New 
 Jersey.\n			\n		\n	\n\n\nEnjoy the exciting live music of Pepe Santana\, an 
 Ecuadorian-born master musician based in New York City\, with Grupo 
 Inkhay\, six musicians who play over two dozen musical instruments a 
 variety of pan-pipes known as "sikus"\, "antaras" or "zampoñas". They also 
 play end-nocthed vertical flutes called kenas\, transverse flutes\, 
 whistles and ocarinas as well as an array of percussion instruments. 
 \n\nSantana emigrated to the United States 38 years ago after the 
 Immigration and Nationality Act of 1965 commemorated in the Paved with 
 Promise suitcase exhibition that will be installed in Montclair Public 
 Library's lobby on July 1 by the Folklife Center of Northern New Jersey. 
 The Andean pan-pipes Santana brought with him from Ecuador and lent to the 
 Folklife Center are part of the display.\n\nSantana has shared the musical 
 traditions of the Andes\, his lifelong passion\, in venues such as the 
 Lincoln Center\, Alice Tully Hall\, and Carnegie Hall\, among many others. 
 His emphasis on age-old sounds and rhythms has defined him as a true 
 spokesman of traditional Andean music. \n\nCo-sponsored by the Folklife 
 Center of Northern New Jersey
LOCATION:Montclair Main - Auditorium\, Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture, Music
UID:LibCal-10306-16742452
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16742452
END:VEVENT
