SUMMARY:Mickalene Thomas: Subverting the Familiar Online NEW
DESCRIPTION:This is a free Adult School class. Click here to register on 
 the Adult School website or register below.\n\nMickalene Thomas has given 
 us vivid and multifaceted artworks—paintings\, collage\, photography\, 
 video\, and site-specific installations. Her work addresses our common 
 perceptions of beauty\, sexuality\, celebrity\, and politics\, and expands 
 and subverts these notions in original and complex ways. The subject of a 
 recent major international tour that began at The Broad in Los Angeles in 
 May of 2024\, traveled to The Barnes Foundation in Philadelphia on October 
 20\, and culminated at The Hayward Gallery in London from February 11 to 
 May 5\, 2025\, Mickalene Thomas has assumed her rightful place among the 
 most important\, original\, and inspiring artists of the 21st 
 century.\n\n“Come Celebrate With Me” is a year-long series of 
 programming honoring 100 years of observing Black history in America. 
 Founded in 1926 by Carter G. Woodson\, Negro History Week evolved into 
 Black History Month\, opening the door for additional annual commemorations 
 such as Juneteenth\, Black Music Month\, Caribbean Heritage Month\, Kwanzaa 
 and more.
LOCATION:Montclair Public Library
ORGANIZER;CN="Montclair Adult School":MAILTO:adultschool@montclairlibrary.org
CATEGORIES:Adult School, Lectures / History & Culture
UID:LibCal-10306-16740762
URL:https://bccls.libcal.com/event/16740762
END:VEVENT
