scend on Leonato’s castle for a few weeks of rest and relaxation after claiming victory in battle. What follows is a witty examination of the nature of love involving trickery\, mistaken identity\, vengeful propositions\, an exuberant masquerade ball\, and a wedding gone horribly wrong. \nAbout Studio Players \nStudio Players (14 Alvin Place\, Montclair\, NJ) is the oldest continually-operating community theatre in Northern New Jersey–offering numerous opportunities for volunteers to participate at all levels (producing\, directing\, designing\, performing\, and technical support) in productions of exciting new plays and beloved classics. Founded in 1937 on the site of an old clock factory\, our non-profit organization is now a staple of Montclair’s ever-growing arts scene\, and we pride ourselves in presenting quality productions featuring groups of artists that reflect the diversity of Montclair and the surrounding communities. For more information\, please visit StudioPlayers.org
